    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start but it feels a bit... safe? maybe a little too concise. \n\nthe editor is actually being a bit of a stickler this time. they said the 'Descriptive Richness' score needs to be higher for the feature section of the mag, otherwise it looks like a quick blurb rather than a full review. \n\ncan you try expanding on the sensory details? maybe go deeper into the texture of the duck or the vibe of the room? just try to make it more evocative and lush, but please—and i mean this—don't just throw a bunch of random adjectives in for the sake of it. i don't want it to look like you're just trying to game that adjective count formula. keep it classy.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
